而卢克说：“不，那不是真的。”

1147
00:50:20.040 --> 00:50:27.680
I knew the reference, but I did get a fan question from kslackish1 who wanted to know if that bit
我知道这个梗，但我确实收到了一位粉丝kslackish1的提问，想知道我做广播公告的那一段

1148
00:50:27.680 --> 00:50:30.780
where I make the announcement was improvised.
是不是即兴发挥的。

1149
00:50:30.920 --> 00:50:33.380
So the Luke line was scripted.
卢克的那句台词是剧本里写的。

1150
00:50:33.500 --> 00:50:36.300
However, I did improvise a little bit.
不过，我确实即兴发挥了一点点。

1151
00:50:36.300 --> 00:50:41.540
So when I say I'm sorry into the mic, that was my fun idea.
所以我对着麦克风说“对不起”的时候，那是我觉得好玩才想出来的点子。

1152
00:50:41.540 --> 00:50:45.540
And it was a little nod to the movie When Harry Met Sally.
那是向电影《当哈利遇上莎莉》致敬的一个小细节。

1153
00:50:46.500 --> 00:50:51.660
So do you remember the scene in When Harry Met Sally when Harry and Sally, they're singing
你还记得《当哈利遇上莎莉》里哈利和莎莉在店里唱卡拉OK的那一幕吗？

1154
00:50:51.660 --> 00:50:53.100
karaoke in the store.
他们在唱《Surrey with a Fringe on Top》。

1155
00:50:53.300 --> 00:50:55.240
They're singing Surrey with a Fringe on Top.
他们在唱《Surrey with a Fringe on Top》。

1156
00:50:55.620 --> 00:51:00.500
And Harry's ex-wife starts to walk up and he stops singing.
然后哈利的前妻走过来，他就不唱了。

1157
00:51:00.800 --> 00:51:04.780
And Meg Ryan is like, oh my gosh, it's my voice.
梅格·瑞恩当时就说，天哪，那是我的声音。

1158
00:51:04.780 --> 00:51:05.720
I have the worst voice.
我的声音太难听了。

1159
00:51:05.720 --> 00:51:07.400
And she's saying it all in the microphone.
她对着麦克风把这些话全说了出来。

1160
00:51:07.580 --> 00:51:12.000
And Harry is like, no, I think I see Helen.
哈利就说，不，我想我看到海伦了。

1161
00:51:12.280 --> 00:51:15.540
And then really loudly into the microphone, Meg Ryan goes, Helen?
然后梅格·瑞恩对着麦克风大声喊道：海伦？

1162
00:51:16.520 --> 00:51:18.600
And it like goes out over the store.
声音传遍了整个商店。

1163
00:51:18.780 --> 00:51:21.400
I always thought that was such a funny bit.
我一直觉得那个桥段特别好笑。

1164
00:51:21.400 --> 00:51:25.700
So I thought I'm going to say I'm sorry into the mic really loudly.
所以我当时想，我也要对着麦克风大声说“对不起”。

1165
00:51:26.740 --> 00:51:28.000
And I don't know.
我也不知道。

1166
00:51:28.440 --> 00:51:32.980
I mean, probably no one would ever think about it.
我是说，可能根本没人会往那方面想。

1167
00:51:33.160 --> 00:51:35.580
But your inspiration for that moment?
但那是你那一刻的灵感来源？

1168
00:51:35.580 --> 00:51:36.460
I love that.
我太喜欢这个了。

1169
00:51:36.580 --> 00:51:37.460
I think that's so sweet.
我觉得这太可爱了。

1170
00:51:37.580 --> 00:51:40.640
I also know how much you love When Harry Met Sally.
而且我知道你有多喜欢《当哈利遇上莎莉》。

1171
00:51:40.780 --> 00:51:42.020
It's one of your favorite movies.
那是你最喜欢的电影之一。

1172
00:51:42.540 --> 00:51:48.320
Lady, when I was in college, I had a three and a half hour drive between St.
亲爱的，我上大学的时候，要在圣路易斯（我父母当时住的地方）和密苏里州的柯克斯维尔之间开车，全程要三个半小时。

1173
00:51:48.460 --> 00:51:52.580
Louis, which is where my parents still lived, and Kirksville, Missouri, which is a little
柯克斯维尔是密苏里州的一个小乡村城镇，我在那里的杜鲁门州立大学上学。

1174
00:51:53.940 --> 00:51:58.500
rural town in Missouri where I went to college at Truman State University.
为了打发时间，我把《当哈利遇上莎莉》录到了磁带上。

1175
00:51:58.500 --> 00:52:05.800
And what I did to pass the time was I recorded When Harry Met Sally onto an audio tape.
然后开车的时候，我就在车里播放这部电影听。

1176
00:52:06.420 --> 00:52:12.800
And then I played the movie back for myself in my car on my drive.
整部电影我从头到尾都能背下来。

1177
00:52:12.800 --> 00:52:16.900
I have that entire movie memorized from beginning to end.
我太爱它了。

1178
00:52:17.140 --> 00:52:18.520
I love it.
我太爱这个了。

1179
00:52:18.740 --> 00:52:18.880
I love that.
我太爱这个了。

1180
00:52:19.120 --> 00:52:20.780
That is the sweetest thing.
这真是太贴心了。

1181
00:52:21.140 --> 00:52:21.460
Yeah.
是啊。

1182
00:52:21.640 --> 00:52:26.780
I recorded on my tape recorder David Letterman's opening monologues.
我以前用录音机录过大卫·莱特曼的开场独白。

1183
00:52:27.040 --> 00:52:30.800
And I would play them back and listen to his opening monologues.
我会反复播放，听他的开场独白。

1184
00:52:31.080 --> 00:52:32.420
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

1185
00:52:32.860 --> 00:52:37.040
Well, you said you wanted to work for a late night talk show.
嗯，你说过你想去深夜脱口秀节目工作。

1186
00:52:37.040 --> 00:52:38.420
I wanted to work in comedy.
我想从事喜剧行业。

1187
00:52:38.640 --> 00:52:40.960
You love, yeah, comedy late night.
你喜欢，没错，深夜喜剧。

1188
00:52:41.300 --> 00:52:41.460
Yeah.
是啊。

1189
00:52:41.860 --> 00:52:42.080
Yeah.
是啊。

1190
00:52:42.780 --> 00:52:43.680
Aw, lady.
噢，亲爱的。

1191
00:52:44.040 --> 00:52:45.660
Look, we were meant to be BFFs.
你看，我们注定要成为好闺蜜。

1192
00:52:45.720 --> 00:52:47.420
We were both driving in our cars.
我们当时都在各自的车里。

1193
00:52:47.840 --> 00:52:48.180
We were.
我们确实是。

1194
00:52:48.320 --> 00:52:54.900
Listening to things we recorded off of our TVs because we're 100 on our tape decks.
听着我们从电视上录下来的东西，因为我们都有一百岁了，还在用磁带播放机。

