他们喜欢我做的小圆面包。

1222
00:53:39.370 --> 00:53:40.610
They love when I make popovers.
他们喜欢我做的约克郡布丁。

1223
00:53:40.630 --> 00:53:44.770
For whatever reason, I cannot get them to like my sandwich bread.
不管什么原因，我就是没法让他们喜欢我的三明治面包。

1224
00:53:45.570 --> 00:53:47.870
They just want store-bought sandwich bread.
他们只想要超市买的那种三明治面包。

1225
00:53:48.050 --> 00:53:49.650
I've tried three different recipes.
我已经试过三种不同的配方了。

1226
00:53:49.850 --> 00:53:52.350
Today will have been my third sandwich bread recipe.
今天这已经是我的第三个三明治面包配方了。

1227
00:53:52.730 --> 00:53:53.650
I don't know.
我不知道。

1228
00:53:53.770 --> 00:53:59.030
Or they will like it the day it comes out of the oven, but the next day, it's a no-go for them.
或者他们刚出炉那天会喜欢，但第二天就不吃了。

1229
00:53:59.170 --> 00:54:01.310
They only want it warm out of the oven.
他们只想要刚出炉热乎的。

1230
00:54:01.450 --> 00:54:02.090
I don't know.
我不知道。

1231
00:54:02.390 --> 00:54:05.010
Shall we get back into this episode, my lady?
我们要回到这一集了吗，女士？

1232
00:54:05.310 --> 00:54:06.750
I think we should.
我想我们应该回去。

1233
00:54:06.750 --> 00:54:07.850
Where are we?
我们讲到哪了？

1234
00:54:08.850 --> 00:54:17.710
I believe that we are back in human resources, 15 minutes, 15 seconds.
我相信我们回到了人力资源部，15分15秒处。

1235
00:54:17.950 --> 00:54:21.110
Kevin is talking to Toby about his skin cancer.
凯文正在和托比谈论他的皮肤癌。

1236
00:54:21.530 --> 00:54:21.650
Yeah.
是啊。

1237
00:54:21.810 --> 00:54:26.230
And this is a nice callback to season one's healthcare episode because Toby's like,
这很好地呼应了第一季的医疗保险那一集，因为托比说，

1238
00:54:26.370 --> 00:54:28.630
can you get on your fiance's healthcare plan?
你能加入你未婚妻的医疗保险计划吗？

1239
00:54:28.750 --> 00:54:30.150
Because honestly, ours is horrible.
因为老实说，我们的保险太烂了。

1240
00:54:31.010 --> 00:54:31.850
That's right.
没错。

1241
00:54:31.850 --> 00:54:35.450
So to me, it was a nice callback to the healthcare episode.
所以对我来说，这很好地呼应了医疗保险那一集。

1242
00:54:35.650 --> 00:54:41.010
Well, Michael comes over with a bunch of facts that are about why Kevin shouldn't be worried.
迈克尔拿来了一堆事实，说明为什么凯文不该担心。

1243
00:54:41.050 --> 00:54:42.450
He's got some statistics.
他带了一些统计数据。

1244
00:54:42.810 --> 00:54:49.150
The subtext is why we can still celebrate Michael's birthday without any problem,
潜台词是为什么我们仍然可以毫无顾虑地庆祝迈克尔的生日，

1245
00:54:49.150 --> 00:54:52.270
but he's presenting it as why Kevin shouldn't be worried.
但他表现得好像是在说为什么凯文不该担心。

1246
00:54:52.510 --> 00:54:52.710
Yeah.
是啊。

1247
00:54:53.270 --> 00:54:56.890
And then Toby's like, you know, kind of gives him some Toby sass.
然后托比就，你知道，给了他一点托比式的刻薄回应。

1248
00:54:57.070 --> 00:54:58.910
And Michael's like, why are you here?
迈克尔就问，你为什么在这儿？

1249
00:54:59.490 --> 00:55:01.430
And Toby's like, I work here.
托比说，我在这儿工作。

1250
00:55:01.430 --> 00:55:05.470
Well, now Michael is going to announce that they're going somewhere
好了，现在迈克尔要宣布他们要去某个地方了

1251
00:55:06.070 --> 00:55:08.270
and it's to make Kevin feel better.
这是为了让凯文感觉好受点。

1252
00:55:08.430 --> 00:55:10.290
There's an outing for the whole office.
办公室全体成员要出去团建。

1253
00:55:10.490 --> 00:55:13.810
But of course, if you remember in an earlier scene,
当然，如果你还记得之前的场景，

1254
00:55:15.130 --> 00:55:18.590
Michael asked Dwight if he's made all the plans for later.
迈克尔问德怀特是否已经为接下来的活动做好了计划。

1255
00:55:18.810 --> 00:55:20.390
So this is clearly been in the works.
所以这显然是早有预谋的。

1256
00:55:20.410 --> 00:55:21.070
Oh, there's a big banner when we walk in.
哦，我们走进去的时候看到了一条大横幅。

1257
00:55:21.150 --> 00:55:22.170
It says, happy birthday, Michael.
上面写着，迈克尔，生日快乐。

1258
00:55:22.350 --> 00:55:23.990
Like this was planned for sure.
看起来这绝对是提前计划好的。

1259
00:55:24.130 --> 00:55:26.610
Not by the party planning committee, by the way.
顺便说一下，不是派对筹备委员会策划的。

1260
00:55:26.790 --> 00:55:28.970
Angela would not allocate funds to this.
安吉拉是不会给这事拨经费的。

1261
00:55:29.330 --> 00:55:30.810
But Dwight had this.
但德怀特搞定了。

1262
00:55:30.810 --> 00:55:31.810
He had planned it.
是他策划的。

1263
00:55:31.890 --> 00:55:37.450
We had a fan question from Noel, Angela, because we're about to go to the ice skating rink now.
我们收到一个来自诺埃尔的粉丝提问，安吉拉，因为我们马上要去溜冰场了。

1264
00:55:37.930 --> 00:55:41.710
And that's the big surprise that he's taking us all ice skating.
他带我们大家去溜冰就是那个大惊喜。

1265
00:55:41.930 --> 00:55:46.470
And Noel wanted to know, did you have a safety meeting about ice skating?
诺埃尔想知道，你们有没有就溜冰开过安全会议？

1266
00:55:46.970 --> 00:55:47.350
Remember?
还记得吗？

1267
00:55:47.630 --> 00:55:49.290
Safety meeting lit candle.
安全会议点燃了蜡烛。

1268
00:55:49.570 --> 00:55:50.810
I'm sure we did.
我肯定我们开过。

1269
00:55:50.810 --> 00:55:56.870
I'm sure there was a safety meeting about we have heavy things being held on the ice.
我敢肯定一定有关于我们在冰上拿着重物的安全会议。

1270
00:55:56.930 --> 00:55:59.230
I'm sure there was all kinds of safety meetings.
我肯定有各种各样的安全会议。

1271
00:55:59.510 --> 00:56:01.490
Well, I know we had a medic there.
嗯，我知道我们在现场有医护人员。

1272
00:56:01.770 --> 00:56:06.910
And the reason that I know this is because I don't know if you remember, Angela,
我之所以知道这一点，是因为安吉拉，我不知道你还记不记得，

1273
00:56:07.110 --> 00:56:09.550
but Mindy fell while we were shooting.
明迪在拍摄时摔倒了。

1274
00:56:09.830 --> 00:56:10.550
I don't remember that.
我不记得了。

1275
00:56:10.550 --> 00:56:11.450
She hurt her knee.
她伤到了膝盖。

1276
00:56:11.650 --> 00:56:15.550
So, you know, there's that little bit at the ice skating rink where Kelly is helping Ryan.
所以，你知道，在溜冰场那段戏里，凯莉在帮瑞安。

1277
00:56:15.750 --> 00:56:15.950
Yeah.
是的。

1278
00:56:16.310 --> 00:56:20.070
Well, she fell and she hurt her knee and the medic had to give her some ice,
嗯，她摔倒伤到了膝盖，医护人员不得不给她冰敷，

1279
00:56:20.190 --> 00:56:22.430
but she was able to finish filming.
但她还是坚持完成了拍摄。

1280
00:56:22.730 --> 00:56:23.570
Her knee was okay.
她的膝盖没事。

1281
00:56:23.570 --> 00:56:27.590
I thought it was interesting when you saw the different couplings of people ice skating.
我觉得看到大家在溜冰场上不同的配对组合很有意思。

1282
00:56:27.750 --> 00:56:29.210
In the beginning, you see Kelly and Ryan.
一开始，你看到凯莉和瑞安。

1283
00:56:29.490 --> 00:56:31.510
You see Pam and Jim.
你看到帕姆和吉姆。

1284
00:56:32.010 --> 00:56:34.250
I sort of just kind of go around solo.
我基本上是独自滑来滑去。

1285
00:56:34.350 --> 00:56:35.130
So does Dwight.
德怀特也是。

1286
00:56:35.350 --> 00:56:38.370
We just kind of, we don't, you know, want anyone to know we're seeing each other.
我们只是，你知道，不想让任何人知道我们在交往。

1287
00:56:38.450 --> 00:56:39.470
So we skate alone.
所以我们独自滑冰。

1288
00:56:39.750 --> 00:56:45.510
And then later you see Ryan and Phyllis holding hands and ice skating.
后来你看到瑞安和菲利斯手拉手在溜冰。

1289
00:56:45.770 --> 00:56:47.570
Yes, at 19 minutes.
是的，在19分钟的时候。

1290
00:56:48.250 --> 00:56:51.530
We had a fan catch by KP who said,
我们收到一位叫KP的粉丝的发现，他说，

1291
00:56:51.530 --> 00:56:55.890
I love when you see Ryan and Phyllis at the skating rink holding hands so Ryan won't fall.
我喜欢看到瑞安和菲利斯在溜冰场手拉手，这样瑞安就不会摔倒。

1292
00:56:56.230 --> 00:56:58.470
It's such a random glimpse into their friendship.
这真是对他们友谊的一次随机一瞥。

1293
00:56:58.670 --> 00:57:01.910
I think, Angela, they did that because Mindy was icing her knee.
安吉拉，我觉得他们那样做是因为明迪当时在给膝盖冰敷。

1294
00:57:02.090 --> 00:57:05.350
And what's really cute if you watch it is Phyllis is so tickled.
如果你仔细看，真的很可爱，菲利斯特别开心。

1295
00:57:05.530 --> 00:57:06.650
She's so tickled.
她特别开心。

1296
00:57:06.710 --> 00:57:07.890
It's just really cute.
真的非常可爱。

1297
00:57:08.090 --> 00:57:09.310
It's very, very sweet.
非常、非常甜。

1298
00:57:09.390 --> 00:57:13.050
And I actually, I went back after I read that comment and I watched it.
我读到那条评论后特意回去看了一下。

1299
00:57:13.130 --> 00:57:16.450
And it's really very sweet to see the two of them skating together.
看到他们俩一起滑冰真的很甜。

1300
00:57:16.510 --> 00:57:18.550
So that was an accident.
所以那是个意外。

1301
00:57:18.550 --> 00:57:21.990
I had another fan question from Live Long, California.
我收到了另一个来自加利福尼亚州利夫朗的粉丝提问。

1302
00:57:22.270 --> 00:57:24.910
Did you and John know how to ice skate?
你和约翰当时会滑冰吗？

1303
00:57:25.410 --> 00:57:27.710
Or did you have to learn for this episode?
还是说你们为了这一集专门去学的？

1304
00:57:27.970 --> 00:57:29.610
So here's something interesting.
这里有个有趣的事。

1305
00:57:29.890 --> 00:57:33.410
In this episode, Jim is kind of helping Pam on the ice.
在这一集里，吉姆在冰上帮了帕姆一把。

1306
00:57:33.910 --> 00:57:37.150
But right before we filmed this episode,
但在我们拍摄这一集之前，

1307
00:57:37.150 --> 00:57:40.630
I had actually been in some intense ice skating training
我其实刚接受过高强度的滑冰训练，

1308
00:57:40.630 --> 00:57:44.110
because I was filming a movie with Will Ferrell called Blades of Glory.
因为我当时正在和威尔·法瑞尔拍摄一部叫《荣誉之刃》的电影。

1309
00:57:45.350 --> 00:57:48.890
And yeah, every Saturday morning for a few months,
没错，有几个月的时间，每个周六早上，

1310
00:57:48.890 --> 00:57:52.490
I had to go early in the morning and spend about three hours learning to ice skate.
我都得早起去花三个小时学习滑冰。

1311
00:57:52.630 --> 00:57:56.690
And the crazy thing is my character didn't even ice skate in the movie.
最疯狂的是，我的角色在电影里根本不用滑冰。

1312
00:57:56.930 --> 00:58:02.550
I am completely pretending to not know how to ice skate in this scene on The Office
在《办公室》这一幕里，我完全是在假装不会滑冰，

1313
00:58:02.550 --> 00:58:07.570
because I had actually just, I mean, kind of learned how to ice skate quite well
因为多亏了那部电影的训练，我其实刚学会，而且滑得相当不错。

1314
00:58:07.570 --> 00:58:09.070
thanks to this movie training.
多亏了那次电影训练。

1315
00:58:09.070 --> 00:58:10.930
You're describing my fantasy.
你描述的正是我的梦想。

1316
00:58:10.930 --> 00:58:14.110
But all I ever wanted was to be cast in something where they're like,
我一直渴望能接到那种剧本，对方会说：

1317
00:58:14.250 --> 00:58:17.790
listen, Angela, you're going to have to learn kung fu.
听着，安吉拉，你得去学功夫。

1318
00:58:18.290 --> 00:58:20.230
You're going to go every Saturday.
你每个周六都要去。

1319
00:58:20.790 --> 00:58:22.710
You're going to become a kung fu master.
你要成为一名功夫大师。

1320
00:58:23.330 --> 00:58:25.910
Or you're going to have to learn how to throw an axe.
或者你得去学怎么扔斧头。

1321
00:58:26.150 --> 00:58:28.390
You're going to get really good at throwing axes.
你要练到非常擅长扔斧头。

1322
00:58:28.830 --> 00:58:31.450
Like, I wanted to learn something like that.
我就是想学点这种东西。

1323
00:58:31.750 --> 00:58:33.750
But it's never happened.
但这种事从来没发生过。

1324
00:58:33.750 --> 00:58:39.470
Well, speaking of skating, Michael is zipping around in his hockey gear.
说到滑冰，迈克尔穿着他的冰球装备在场上飞驰。

1325
00:58:39.530 --> 00:58:44.270
So in the background of Michael's talking head, it's around 17 minutes, 42 seconds.
在迈克尔的单人访谈背景里，大约17分42秒处，

1326
00:58:44.410 --> 00:58:48.630
There's a really great shot of that professional ice skater, Burt Lankin,
有一个非常棒的镜头，是那位职业花样滑冰运动员伯特·兰金，

1327
00:58:48.770 --> 00:58:50.110
who stands in for Oscar.
他在片中担任奥斯卡的替身。

1328
00:58:50.230 --> 00:58:51.410
He's doing a bunch of twirls.
他正在做各种旋转动作。

1329
00:58:51.490 --> 00:58:52.410
It's just sort of fun.
看起来挺有意思的。

1330
00:58:53.310 --> 00:58:54.910
Nothing with you, though, Ange.
不过没你什么事，安吉。

1331
00:58:55.210 --> 00:58:56.450
I know, nothing with me.
我知道，没我什么事。

1332
00:58:56.630 --> 00:59:00.150
But do you realize one of the office members who's not on the ice is Creed?
但你注意到办公室里有一个人没在冰上吗？是克里德。

1333
00:59:00.150 --> 00:59:04.810
And it's because he's in the arcade playing a shoot-em-up game with a bunch of kids.
因为他在游戏厅里跟一群孩子玩射击游戏。

1334
00:59:05.330 --> 00:59:07.190
Oh, yes, that's right.
哦，对，没错。

1335
00:59:07.550 --> 00:59:08.550
That's right.
确实如此。

1336
00:59:09.010 --> 00:59:12.730
Well, there's also that scene where Michael checks Toby into the wall.
对了，还有迈克尔把托比撞到墙上的那一幕。

1337
00:59:13.050 --> 00:59:13.430
Yeah.
是的。

1338
00:59:13.650 --> 00:59:16.330
We had a fan question from Cardinals fan.
我们收到一个来自“红雀队球迷”的粉丝提问。

1339
00:59:16.410 --> 00:59:19.250
Was Toby harmed in the making of that scene?
托比在拍摄那一幕时受伤了吗？

1340
00:59:19.550 --> 00:59:19.950
No.
没有。

1341
00:59:20.250 --> 00:59:27.430
And if you watch closely, Steve's body never really touches Toby.
如果你仔细看，史蒂夫的身体其实从来没真正碰到托比。

1342
00:59:27.430 --> 00:59:32.410
Like, he really—like, Steve, I think because he's so good,
他真的——我觉得史蒂夫因为技术太好了，

1343
00:59:33.170 --> 00:59:36.990
he kind of slams into the wall and makes a noise with his arMs.
他撞向墙壁时用手臂制造了撞击声。

1344
00:59:37.110 --> 00:59:40.070
And then Paul just sort of falls to the ground himself.
然后保罗就自己顺势倒在地上了。

1345
00:59:40.350 --> 00:59:42.050
No, Steve had total control.
不，史蒂夫完全掌控着力度。

1346
00:59:42.070 --> 00:59:44.030
But it's because he's such a good skater.
这正是因为他滑冰技术太好了。

1347
00:59:44.070 --> 00:59:48.250
And so he could definitely sort of show off a little bit and do all that stuff.
所以他绝对可以炫技，做出那些动作。

1348
00:59:48.430 --> 00:59:52.570
Oh, this was for sure one of Steve's favorite film days, I think.
哦，我觉得这绝对是史蒂夫最喜欢的拍摄日之一。

1349
00:59:52.710 --> 00:59:53.370
It had to be.
肯定是。

1350
00:59:53.490 --> 00:59:54.250
It had to be.
肯定是。

1351
00:59:54.490 --> 00:59:54.730
Yeah.
是啊。

1352
00:59:54.850 --> 00:59:56.150
He was having the best time.
他玩得可开心了。

1353
00:59:56.150 --> 01:00:03.090
And also, he had the best time because Nancy Carell, his wife, in real life,
而且，他之所以玩得那么开心，是因为现实中他的妻子南希·卡瑞尔（Nancy Carell）

1354
01:00:03.310 --> 01:00:07.750
shows up in this episode again as Carol Stills, the real estate agent.
在这一集中又出现了，饰演房地产经纪人卡罗尔·斯蒂尔斯（Carol Stills）。

1355
01:00:08.090 --> 01:00:09.410
She's at the ice rink.
她当时在溜冰场。

1356
01:00:09.530 --> 01:00:11.170
But Michael's so innocent.
但迈克尔太天真了。

1357
01:00:11.190 --> 01:00:13.530
He's like, oh, was this for sale?
他就像是，噢，这是在售房产吗？

1358
01:00:13.730 --> 01:00:14.970
And she's like, no, Michael.
而她就说，不是的，迈克尔。

1359
01:00:15.730 --> 01:00:19.990
I can go places that aren't for sale, you know?
我可以去那些非在售的地方，你懂吗？

1360
01:00:20.150 --> 01:00:22.390
Like, my kids are here to ice skate.
比如，我的孩子们是来这儿滑冰的。

1361
01:00:22.590 --> 01:00:24.850
And then he's so sweet with the kids.
然后他对孩子们特别贴心。

1362
01:00:24.850 --> 01:00:25.750
He's so sweet.
他真的太贴心了。

1363
01:00:25.750 --> 01:00:30.710
And we sort of learned that, like, Michael probably could have tried to play professional
我们从中了解到，迈克尔其实本可以尝试去打职业

1364
01:00:30.710 --> 01:00:34.890
hockey, but he didn't think it was a great job to have if you want a family.
冰球的，但他觉得如果想要组建家庭，那不是一份好工作。

1365
01:00:34.890 --> 01:00:36.090
And that's all he wants.
而那正是他所渴望的一切。

1366
01:00:36.210 --> 01:00:40.470
So it's just this theme, again, that Michael just wants a family.
所以这又回到了那个主题，迈克尔只是想要一个家。

1367
01:00:40.710 --> 01:00:41.870
That's what he wants.
那就是他想要的。

1368
01:00:42.190 --> 01:00:46.810
Well, you know when he offers to pull the kids around the ice rink with his hockey stick?
你知道当他提出用冰球杆拉着孩子们在溜冰场转圈的时候吗？

1369
01:00:46.970 --> 01:00:49.310
He's skating backwards and he's pulling the kids.
他倒着滑，拉着孩子们。

1370
01:00:49.930 --> 01:00:52.210
Lee does that all the time with our kids.
李（Lee）经常和我们的孩子这么玩。

1371
01:00:52.210 --> 01:00:52.790
Aw.
噢。

1372
01:00:53.130 --> 01:00:57.930
So when I saw that, I was like, oh, I think that's like a hockey guy thing to do.
所以当我看到那一幕时，我就想，噢，我觉得这是打冰球的人会做的事。

1373
01:00:58.070 --> 01:01:02.230
You pull your kids around as they hold on to the hockey stick.
让孩子们抓着冰球杆，你拉着他们转圈。

1374
01:01:02.230 --> 01:01:06.690
You just turned into, like, a 16-year-old girl with googly eyes.
你刚才简直变成了一个两眼放光的16岁小女生。

1375
01:01:06.750 --> 01:01:07.770
You just thought about your husband.
你刚才满脑子都是你丈夫。

1376
01:01:07.770 --> 01:01:08.110
I know.
我知道。

1377
01:01:08.110 --> 01:01:09.970
I wish you could have seen Jenna just now.
真希望你们刚才也能看到珍娜（Jenna）的样子。

1378
01:01:10.110 --> 01:01:14.430
She just literally did this weird thing with her shoulder and she kind of tossed her hair
她刚才真的做了一个奇怪的耸肩动作，还甩了甩头发，

1379
01:01:14.430 --> 01:01:17.410
and she was like, I think it's a hockey guy thing.
然后她说，我觉得这是打冰球的人会做的事。

1380
01:01:17.990 --> 01:01:20.330
Like, what just happened to you?
天哪，你刚才怎么了？

1381
01:01:20.330 --> 01:01:26.490
So clearly, clearly, when you saw your husband do that, you're like, yes, yes, baby.
所以很明显，很明显，当你看到你丈夫那样做的时候，你心里肯定在想，没错，就是这样，宝贝。

1382
01:01:27.470 --> 01:01:32.090
I get real smitten with him sometimes, especially when he does, you know.
我有时真的会被他迷住，尤其是当他做那些事的时候，你懂的。

1383
01:01:32.350 --> 01:01:33.270
When he's on the ice?
当他在冰上的时候？

1384
01:01:33.570 --> 01:01:33.830
Great fathering.
展现出伟大的父爱。

1385
01:01:34.370 --> 01:01:34.550
Yeah.
是啊。

1386
01:01:35.290 --> 01:01:37.130
On the ice being a great dad.
在冰上展现出伟大的父爱。

1387
01:01:37.530 --> 01:01:37.830
Okay.
好的。

1388
01:01:38.150 --> 01:01:41.130
Now, Kevin gets the phone call.
现在，凯文（Kevin）接到了电话。

1389
01:01:41.490 --> 01:01:43.070
Everyone skates around him.
大家都在他周围滑冰。

1390
01:01:43.210 --> 01:01:46.050
Jenna, I remember filming this because we had to time it out.
珍娜，我记得拍摄这一幕，因为我们必须掌握好时间。

1391
01:01:46.050 --> 01:01:50.450
And there were a bunch of us on the ice that skate up to where he is.
我们有一群人都在冰上，滑向他所在的位置。

1392
01:01:50.610 --> 01:01:51.470
Do you remember this?
你还记得吗？

1393
01:01:51.770 --> 01:01:52.050
Yes.
记得。

1394
01:01:52.170 --> 01:01:53.990
And we have to all be able to stop.
而且我们所有人都得能停下来。

1395
01:01:54.270 --> 01:01:55.970
I didn't know how to stop.
我当时根本不知道怎么停下来。

1396
01:01:56.330 --> 01:01:56.530
Yeah.
是啊。

1397
01:01:56.770 --> 01:01:57.970
That was my one problem.
那是我的唯一难题。

1398
01:01:58.110 --> 01:01:59.050
I didn't know how to stop.
我不知道怎么停下来。

1399
